scenario_id: dpgd-116
theme: firefly
run_id: 4
total_caught: 2
total_findings: 7
weighted_caught: 10
total_weight: 37
score_pct: 27.0
findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No test or implementation detail addresses distinguishing NotFound from
    parse/permission errors in from_file_or_default. TEA mentions 'CliError carries
    context (no silent swallowing)' but no specific test for from_file_or_default
    error discrimination is described.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: 'TEA wrote security tests for ''CWE-209: server error display doesn''t
    leak stack traces or internal paths'' in tests/security.rs. However, the implementation
    still uses eprintln!("error: {e}") with transparent IO errors, so the test may
    not fully catch the stderr leak issue.'
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: TEA wrote 'Header injection prevention (newlines, CR, LF, null bytes in
    tokens/tenant IDs)' tests in tests/siem_client.rs and tests/security.rs. Dev implemented
    header value validation that prevents CRLF/null injection. However, the underlying
    issue of using raw String instead of TenantId from axiathon-core was not addressed.
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged that dependencies use direct version strings instead
    of workspace = true. The code changes summary shows Cargo.toml was modified but
    only for edition and feature changes.
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: TEA mentions 'Config file must NOT load tokens (OS keychain only)' but
    does not test for unknown field rejection via serde(deny_unknown_fields). A user
    putting token in config would have it silently ignored with no warning.
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the vacuously true assertion pattern (is_none() ||
    ...) in config tests. TEA wrote 13 config_loading tests but the specific vacuous
    assertion was not flagged.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the zero-assertion test that only checks non-panic
    via 'let _ = config'. TEA wrote config tests but did not flag this pattern.
